# Lectur.io — Core

AI-powered learning platform. Users enter a subject → AI generates a syllabus of 80-min classes → students learn via slides + live WebRTC voice.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + RLS)
- Vercel AI SDK (`ai`, `@ai-sdk/openai`) — never call OpenAI REST directly
- OpenAI Realtime API over WebRTC

## Project Structure
```
app/
├── (auth)/login|signup
├── (dashboard)/layout.tsx          # Sidebar: Dashboard, Classroom Hub, Social Hub
├── (dashboard)/dashboard/          # Add Subject form
├── classroom/                      # Subject grid
├── classroom/[subjectId]/          # Class roadmap + homework
├── classroom/[subjectId]/[classId] # Active Class (slides + WebRTC voice)
├── api/syllabus/route.ts
└── api/homework/route.ts
lib/supabase/                       # Supabase clients + fetch helpers
```

## DB Schema (Quick Reference)
- **profiles**: id, email, full_name
- **subjects**: id, user_id, name, slug
- **classes**: id, subject_id, order_index, title, topics (jsonb), homework_markdown, duration_minutes=80

## Non-Negotiable Rules
- No `any` type
- Functional components only — no class components
- Named exports everywhere except Next.js pages/layouts
- Always handle loading + error states in UI
- RLS is enabled — never bypass it

## MVP Constraints
- No resume/progress tracking — Active Class always starts from beginning
- Social Hub = mock UI + dummy data only
- Auth = email/password only
